<title>CANADA: CBRS reaffirms Provigo ratings.</title>
<headline>CBRS reaffirms Provigo ratings.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Bond Rating Service said on Friday that it reaffirmed the debt and preferred share ratings of Provigo Inc, with a stable rating outlook.</p>
<p>The rating agency said it reaffirmed Provigo's unsecured debentures at B++, its preferred shares at P-3 and its commercial paper at A-2.</p>
<p>Although the company's margins have suffered in fiscal 1997 because of intense competition and labour unrest in Ontario, cash flow is improving and equity will gradually begin to recover on the strength of improved retained earnings, CBRS said.</p>
<p>Write-offs at Provigo have been completed, no further lease liabilities are outstanding with respect to asset disposition, and all operations remain profitable, CBRS said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
</text>
